{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>חרדת</b> — a verb falling upon the noun חרדה, if it is the language, like ויאבד את לב מתנה. That is, the dread of a man — he who frightens after the dread — gives a snare to his soul." "<b>ישוגב</b> — HaShem will set him on high because of the one who frightens. Another interpretation: HaShem will cause him to tremble and give him the snare that he sets to catch the poor. Another interpretation: a man fears and does not place his trust in HaShem — what he fears will come upon him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:28.983234321Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}